        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a62a5f34-0057-5891-a3e3-0bc636428696",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Užupis, Freetown Christiania, Belmontas, Rasos, Vilnia River, Paris, Copenhagen\n- Topics: artists, bohemic atmosphere, laissez-faire atmosphere, district comparisons, public closure\n\nFacts:\n- Užupis has been popular with artists for some time.\n- Užupis has been compared to Montmartre in Paris because of its bohemic and laissez-faire atmosphere.\n- Užupis has also been compared to Freetown Christiania in Copenhagen because of its bohemic and laissez-faire atmosphere.\n- In April 2011, residents of Freetown Christiania temporarily closed it to the public while discussions with the Danish government about its future continued.\n- After the temporary closure in April 2011, Freetown Christiania re-opened to the public.\n- Belmontas is located in the Rasos area on the right bank of the Vilnia River, east of Užupis.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
